This product includes software developed for the tnl project.

Comment-preserving tsconfig edits use HuJSON (BSD-3-Clause), developed by
Tailscale Inc. and contributors.

Third-party license terms and notices are provided in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.

Operational metrics, tracing, and logs use OpenTelemetry Go, its OTLP/HTTP and
Prometheus exporters, and the OpenTelemetry Prometheus bridge (Apache-2.0),
developed by the OpenTelemetry Authors. Prometheus metric name translation uses
otlptranslator (Apache-2.0), developed by the Prometheus Authors.

DNS automation, publisher identity bootstrap (Secrets Manager and STS), and
publisher target discovery (EKS, RDS and STS) use the AWS SDK for Go v2 and Smithy
for Go (Apache-2.0), developed by Amazon Web Services and contributors.

Publisher target TLS includes public Amazon RDS root certificates published by
Amazon Web Services at https://truststore.pki.rds.amazonaws.com/global/global-bundle.pem.
The pinned source digest and regional certificate digests are distributed in
internal/rdsroots/bundles.json in the source tree and embedded in the binary.

The Python ASGI binding directly depends on HTTPX, Starlette, Uvicorn, and
websockets (BSD-3-Clause). Their distributions provide their license texts.

Kubernetes client configuration and exec credentials use the official client-go
and apimachinery API types (Apache-2.0), developed by the Kubernetes Authors.

The Node connection helper uses Undici (MIT), developed by the Undici team and
contributors, for scoped native HTTPS dispatch without changing application headers.

The GitHub connection action uses the official Actions toolkit (MIT), developed
by GitHub, and Zod (MIT), developed by Colin McDonnell and contributors. The
committed action bundles include their dependency license texts in connect/dist.
